{B} I've submitted this to the dev team, but I'm interested to see if this has 
{B} happened to anyone else.

Yes.

{B} The next time you're playing, drop something on a sink and try to kick it
{B} off.  It doesn't work for me.  No kick, no "You kick at empty space", no
{B} nothing.

I noticed that one many moons ago.  I guess my bug report must have gotten lost
somewhere though ;-).

I looked into (briefly) what it would take to fix this problem.  Seems that
no real good code was written to implment kicking an object.  What happenes
is the throwing code is used and the object is "backed up" one square and
then "thrown" from there.

Well, it turns out that if you throw an object over a sink it will "sink"
right there, and stop.  Hence, you can never kick an object off a sink
and you never see it move, but the game thinks it's done something.

BTW, this was how I learned about this "sinking objects" property of sinks.

Fixing it was just about as ugly as the code, and had to do with mucking
with the xbhity() functions.  I shudder at the thought.

{B} I'm running 3.0j on an Atari ST.  Am I an aberration?

Certainly not.

